### 2026-09-16 · HANDOVER_dds3_interactive_timeseries_embed_and_fhy_shy_split.md

**Scope.** V2 per-student report time-series. Two features, both additive; `_addTimeSeriesPageV2` unchanged. `boh2_dds2_dds3_utils.py`, backup `_bak/boh2_dds2_dds3_utils.py.bak_20260916_004355`. Reuses `student_report_html_utils.py` (unchanged) + `_assets/echarts.min.js`.

**Interactive embed (DDS3 default).** The static scatter piled every session's 3-digit item codes as text — worst for DDS3. Now, for cohorts in `INTERACTIVE_TS_COHORTS=("DDS3",)`, a **self-contained interactive ECharts HTML is embedded inside the PDF** as a file attachment (`pdf.attachments[name]` via `pikepdf`) with an on-page `/FileAttachment` **paperclip** annotation on the chart page; the printable page shows a clean, **label-free** preview + a callout. Hover reveals code/score/GR·ES/assessor/clinic; code filter (`5xx`, `4*`, `011`) with "N of M"; FHY/SHY tabs; rolling-avg(3). Interactive **data comes from `student_report_html_utils._timeseriesBlock`** and ECharts from `_sh._loadEcharts` → numbers can't drift from the HTML report or the PDF. A PDF page can't run hover in any mainstream viewer, so interactivity lives in the attachment (opens in a browser); one file to send.

**FHY/SHY split (all cohorts).** `_v2SplitFhyShy` splits a stream at `TS_SPLIT_DATE=15 Jun 2026` (Melbourne): FHY before, SHY on/after — **two segments only when both halves have forms**. Static path (`_addTimeSeriesPageV2Split`) reuses `_addTimeSeriesPageV2` once per segment on **separate pages** (PageBreak between) so the ES/GR rubric panels split too; interactive path uses tabs. Applies to Sim and Clinic.

